# Rust / Tauri (`src-tauri`)

- Match surrounding error style: `Result<T, String>` on `#[tauri::command]` fn; `anyhow::Result` / `Box<dyn Error>` inside internal helpers.
- Module layout: `src-tauri/src/lib.rs`（shell + `generate_handler!`）、`vault.rs`（macOS Keychain secrets via `security` CLI, service `plos`）、`llm/`（`commands.rs` `manager.rs` `models.rs` `sidecar.rs`）。
- New command: implement in the owning module → register in `lib.rs` `generate_handler!` → call with `invoke` from `src/`. Registered commands: `app_status`、`llm_*`（list/download/cancel/delete/generate/default/status）、`vault_*`（set/get/delete secret）。
- Rust → UI: `app.emit("event-name", payload)` and `listen` in hooks/services; keep payloads `Serialize`/`Deserialize` and mirrored as TS types next to the invoke caller.
- Sidecar: local-model helper binary lifecycle lives in `llm/sidecar.rs`; do not block the main thread on downloads (progress via `llm_download`/events).
- vault is **macOS-only**（`security` CLI）；pure-browser preview (`isTauri` guard) must not touch these commands.
- Do not grow a file already over 700 lines; split by responsibility first.
- Comments in 中文/English — follow the module you edit (repo defaults to 中文).

